The 1919–20 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 32nd season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish Football League]] and the [[Scottish Cup]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1920/celtic1920.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1919-20|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref>

Celtic finished their league campaign runners-up, three points below Rangers in the table. In the Scottish Cup, which was played for the first time since [[1913–14 Scottish Cup|1913-14]], Celtic failed to retain the trophy as they lost in the fourth round to Rangers away, 1-0.

Celtic won both the [[Glasgow Cup]] and the [[Glasgow Charity Cup]] this season, defeating [[Partick Thistle F.C.|Partick Thistle]] and [[Queen's Park F.C.|Queen's Park]] respectively 1-0 in both finals at [[Hampden Park]].

